1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,728
Seventeen percent of U.S. teens say they
often or sometimes can't finish homework

2
00:00:05,778 --> 00:00:09,283
because they lack reliable computer or
internet access.

3
00:00:09,333 --> 00:00:11,950
That's from Pew Research Center, 2018.

4
00:00:12,000 --> 00:00:16,582
ShareSafe Practice is digital-safety
lessons for students like Maya, a seventh

5
00:00:16,632 --> 00:00:21,213
grader on a library computer with an old
phone at home.

6
00:00:21,263 --> 00:00:27,529
No account, no name, and nothing saved
after she closes the tab, unless she
chooses

7
00:00:27,579 --> 00:00:27,950
to.

8
00:00:28,000 --> 00:00:30,867
Everything works from the keyboard.

9
00:00:30,917 --> 00:00:36,700
She picks Permission to Learn and starts a
six-question pre-check.

10
00:00:36,750 --> 00:00:41,950
No hints here, it just shows where she
begins.

11
00:00:42,000 --> 00:00:52,266
The lesson opens on a confusing 403
Forbidden screen, then explains it in
plain

12
00:00:52,316 --> 00:00:53,003
language.

13
00:00:53,053 --> 00:01:02,582
Then she practises least privilege: who
can view or edit a class roster.

14
00:01:02,632 --> 00:01:09,950
If she grants too much access, the
feedback says so.

15
00:01:10,000 --> 00:01:17,362
Students can make the text bigger, switch
to high contrast, or turn on plain

16
00:01:17,412 --> 00:01:17,891
language.

17
00:01:17,941 --> 00:01:24,244
A language switcher sets Spanish,
including the lesson, and updates the page

18
00:01:24,294 --> 00:01:27,950
language so a screen reader switches too.

19
00:01:28,000 --> 00:01:34,472
Before leaving the library, Maya gets her
resume code, or scans the QR with her

20
00:01:34,522 --> 00:01:34,907
phone.

21
00:01:34,957 --> 00:01:41,863
It carries her progress and which pack she
was in, with no account and no server.

22
00:01:41,913 --> 00:01:47,950
The last two characters catch typos, not
forgery, and the app says so honestly.

23
00:01:48,000 --> 00:01:55,863
The first load is about twenty-eight
kilobytes, and packs are cached after one

24
00:01:55,913 --> 00:01:56,472
visit.

25
00:01:56,522 --> 00:02:01,950
So at home, with no internet, it still
works.

26
00:02:02,000 --> 00:02:09,298
On the shared computer, End session wipes
everything the app stored, including the

27
00:02:09,348 --> 00:02:14,950
offline copy if she wants, and confirms
what it removed.

28
00:02:15,000 --> 00:02:17,200
Then the post-check shows her growth.

29
00:02:17,250 --> 00:02:22,450
Teachers can build a pack, watch the byte
count, and print a QR handout.

30
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:27,325
Lighthouse scores a hundred in every
category, axe finds no violations, and
real

31
00:02:27,375 --> 00:02:29,200
screen reader testing is next.

32
00:02:29,250 --> 00:02:29,950
ShareSafe Practice.
